# B4 -- daily score_live.py monitoring (baseline_system_architecture.md
# item 46). This is a PROPOSED line, NOT installed on this machine as of
# this commit -- review the timing note below, then install with the
# command at the bottom once approved. Referenced from CLAUDE.md so
# anyone reading the project docs finds this file, not just this comment.
#
# TIMING: 06:30 local time, weekdays only (NYSE-holiday/weekend detection
# happens inside monitor_score_live.py itself, not here -- this line just
# needs to fire on every calendar weekday). This machine's local zone is
# America/Chicago (confirmed via `timedatectl`: UTC-5 CDT / UTC-6 CST).
# NYSE closes 4:00pm ET, which is always 3:00pm local here -- Eastern and
# Central both observe DST, so the 1-hour offset never changes. 6:30am the
# next morning is a ~15.5 hour buffer after the prior trading day's close:
# src/data_pipeline/fetch_live.py and fetch_training.py both request
# `auto_adjust=False` (the raw price that actually printed, not a
# dividend/split-adjusted figure computed later), and Yahoo Finance
# typically has that raw daily bar available within minutes to a couple
# hours of the close -- 15.5 hours is a comfortable margin, not a tight
# one. cron runs on the system's local time by default (no CRON_TZ set
# here), so "6:30am" tracks local wall-clock automatically across DST
# transitions with no separate adjustment needed.
#
# Before STOCK_LIST/WINDOW_START_DATE are populated (baseline_system_
# architecture.md §5, "Blocked on External Input"), this line runs
# score_live.py, which cleanly fails its own _preflight check and logs
# that -- expected, not an error in this line. It becomes a real live run
# automatically, with no change needed here, the day both are set.
#
# INSTALL (appends one line to this user's existing crontab -- does NOT
# replace it):
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; echo; grep '^30 6' "ops/monitor_score_live.crontab") | crontab -
#
# VERIFY the installed line still matches this file (run any time):
#   diff <(crontab -l | grep monitor_score_live) <(grep monitor_score_live "ops/monitor_score_live.crontab")
#   -- or just: bash scripts/verify_crontab.sh
#
# REMOVE:
#   crontab -e   # delete the one matching line by hand, save, exit
30 6 * * 1-5 cd "/home/blueman1818/Projects/gen alg + XGB" && "/home/blueman1818/.venv/bin/python3" -m scripts.monitor_score_live >> "/home/blueman1818/Projects/gen alg + XGB/data/processed/live_monitor_logs/cron_stdout.log" 2>&1
